00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:19.108
I wasn't in a bar.
我不在酒吧里。

00:00:19.108 --> 00:00:28.379
I was in my office, but across the office, even though I swore I was going to be single for a while, I locked eyes with the woman who is now my wife.
我在办公室，但在办公室的另一头，尽管我发誓要单身一段时间，但我却和那个如今成为我妻子的女人四目相对。

00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:28.879
wife.
我妻子。

00:00:28.879 --> 00:00:42.758
I was already a huge himmium fan and always identified with Ted, somebody who felt deeply and got hurt badly and fell in love fast and wanted to skip the dating stuff to be good at the relationship stuff but maybe didn't want to admit that to myself at the time.
我当时已经是《老爸老妈浪漫史》的超级粉丝，总是把自己代入泰德——一个感情深沉、深受伤害、坠入爱河极快，想跳过约会阶段直接进入恋爱状态的人，也许当时我还没法对自己承认这一点。

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:58.437
And so my wife and I spent several years after that moment with this really tight knit group having our adventures around the city being young being in our 20s and then we had our first child in 2018 and our second a few years later and this brings me to this underexplored way we watch the show.
所以在那之后的好几年里，我和妻子跟这个紧密的小圈子一起在城市里探险，享受年轻的20多岁时光；接着我们在2018年迎来了第一个孩子，几年后又有了第二个，这让我想到了我们观看这部剧的一种未曾被充分探讨的方式。

00:00:58.437 --> 00:01:03.575
There's a phrase you you hear about when you become a new parent, the phrase is loss of identity.
当你成为新手父母时，你会听到这样一个词，叫做“自我丧失”。

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.340
As a parent, you experience a loss of identity.
作为一个父母，你会经历自我的丧失。

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:14.900
And for all the happiness you feel, all the love and fulfillment you receive, you also mourn pieces of yourself that you don't have time or energy to access or that you have to leave behind.
带着你所感受到的所有快乐、所有的爱与成就感，你同时也在悼念那些你不再有时间和精力去触及，或者不得不抛下的部分的自己。

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.420
You feel a loss of identity.
你会感到自我丧失。

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:25.700
And I often think about my days roaming the city with all my friends, daydreaming about the future or just the infinite hours we had at our disposal after brunch on a Saturday.
我常常想起当年和所有朋友在城市里闲逛的日子，幻想着未来，或者只是我们在周六早午餐后可以随意支配的无限时间。

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:36.400
And watching himium today hits different for me because it gives me access to a version of myself, to a major source of my identity, which honestly has been lost as I grew older and became a parent.
如今再看《老爸老妈浪漫史》对我有种完全不同的触动，因为它让我得以重温过去的自己，重温我自我认同的一个主要源泉——说实话，随着我年龄增长并为人父母，这部分已经丢失了。

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.060
